century.\nThe Machiavellians\n1943 book by James Burnham\nThe Machiavellians \n\nTitle page for The Machiavellians: Defenders of Freedom (1943)\n\nAuthor | James Burnham\nLanguage | English\nPublisher | John Day Company\n\nPublication date\n\n | 1943\nPublication place | United States\nPages | 270\nThe Machiavellians: Defenders of Freedom is a 1943 book by the American writer James Burnham.\n## Summary\n\nThe book evokes theorists of elites and power structures, notably Dante Alighieri and Niccolò Machiavelli in the Renaissance period, and Gaetano Mosca, Robert Michels and Vilfredo Pareto in the 20th century. Using their theories, Burnham assesses the contemporary elites of the United States. He concludes that they have become weak, inflexible and bound to American liberalism in ways that erode liberty.\n## Reception\n\nKirkus Reviews called the book stimulating and provocative, but wrote that \"those who would profit most probably won't read it\".\n## References\n*  Hook, Sidney (1988). \"On James Burnham' s The Machiavellians\". Society. 25: 68–70. doi:10.1007/BF02695652. \n*  Huse, H. R. (1943). \"Reviewed Work: The Machiavellians James Burnham\". Southern Economic Journal. 10 (1): 74–76. doi:10.2307/1053407. \n*  \"The Machiavellians: Defenders of Freedom\". The Atlantic. June 1943. Retrieved 16 December 2025. \n*  \"The Machiavellians\". Kirkus Reviews. June 15, 1943. Retrieved 16 December 2025.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Machiavellians - Defenders of Freedom. - Burnham, James, 1905-1987 - 1963 - Chicago - Regnery - Anna's Archive | PDF | Politics | Social Science (https://www.scribd.com/document/666608660/The-Machiavellians-Defenders-of-Freedom-Burnham-James-1905-1987-1963-Chicago-Regnery-Anna-s-Archive)\nciteturn2772search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 63.8 years ago; Crawled: 2.4 years ago; THE MACHIAVELLIANS ... COPYRIGHT, 1943, BY JAMES BURNHAM ... publisher, The John Day Company, Inc. ... Machiav